; vim:ft=scheme
;; Loopback self-dial. mtplx.sb and sushi.sb import this as NET_SELF_SB
;; in TCP serve mode. Both check their own listen port before starting;
;; MTPLX's max-fan watchdog also polls /health. server.sb kills outbound connects with
;; SIGKILL, so this grant is necessary. NET_SELF is "localhost:PORT" —
;; the same address the serving personality permits to bind, and no
;; other outbound target. Socket mode and tune import net-none.sb here
;; instead: they make no connect (name resolution of a .sock path fails
;; first).
(allow network-outbound (remote tcp (param "NET_SELF")))
